%% Figure 3: Data flow of the forkdiff-audit tool.
flowchart LR
    In1["Input:<br/>candidate fork URL"]:::input
    In2["Input:<br/>upstream URL"]:::input

    In1 --> Clone1["git clone --depth=200<br/>candidate -> /tmp/candidate"]
    In2 --> Clone2["git clone --depth=200<br/>upstream -> /tmp/upstream"]

    Clone1 --> Walk1["os.walk<br/>compute SHA-256<br/>per file"]
    Clone2 --> Walk2["os.walk<br/>compute SHA-256<br/>per file"]

    Walk1 --> Diff["Set diff:<br/>added = candidate - upstream<br/>removed = upstream - candidate<br/>changed = same path, diff sha"]
    Walk2 --> Diff

    Diff --> Sniff["sniff() per added file<br/>(first 8 bytes: PE/ELF/ZIP/PNG/...)"]

    Sniff --> Verdict{"Any binary<br/>additions?"}
    Verdict -->|Yes| Susp["VERDICT: SUSPICIOUS<br/>exit code 1"]:::susp
    Verdict -->|No, any diff| Review["VERDICT: REVIEW<br/>exit code 2"]:::review
    Verdict -->|No diff at all| Clean["VERDICT: CLEAN<br/>exit code 0"]:::clean

    Susp --> Report["Human-readable report:<br/>+ added files<br/>~ changed files<br/>- removed files<br/>! flagged binaries"]:::output
    Review --> Report
    Clean --> Report

    classDef input fill:#cce5ff,stroke:#004085,color:#000
    classDef output fill:#d6d8db,stroke:#1b1e21,color:#000
    classDef susp fill:#f8d7da,stroke:#721c24,color:#000
    classDef review fill:#fff3cd,stroke:#856404,color:#000
    classDef clean fill:#d4edda,stroke:#155724,color:#000
